      "stop_reason": "end_turn",
      "tool_uses": [],
      "assistant_text": "According to [[credential-scoping]], the Anthropic API key is injected into the **environment of the spawned Ingest agent child process**, immediately before that process starts. The key is loaded from a git-ignored \u0060.env\u0060 file by a local secrets loader at startup.\n\nThe page emphasizes that this injection happens only in the child process environment \u2014 the Hub\u0027s own process environment is never mutated. This design ensures that if the Hub process is compromised, it cannot leak the credential by inspecting its own environment variables, since the key exists only inside the short-lived child process that actually calls the Anthropic API.\n\nThe same scoping model also applies to the Query agent process, which receives the credential through the same mechanism.",
